; Provider-route aggregate family, 1 of 3 — rejections of the *schema*,
; raised before any document is looked at, so every host that can load a
; manifest replays them whether or not it can run an extractor.
;
; `(cross-ref :provider …)` draws a cross-ref's member set from a declared
; `(cross-ref-provider …)` instead of from each target instance's
; `:name-key` symbol. Here the manifest declares no provider at all, so
; `:provider glsl-uniforms` resolves to nothing — the provider-route twin
; of `unknown_cross_ref_target`.
;
; The document deliberately instantiates nothing: with the provider
; unresolved there is no member set to reference, and a reference would
; only add a second, downstream diagnostic on top of the root cause.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0" :sjon "1.2"
  (form :name shader
    (key :name name :type symbol :optional false)
    (key :name src :type string :optional false))

  (value-kind :name uniform-name
    :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target shader :provider glsl-uniforms))

  (form :name bind
    (key :name uniform :type uniform-name :optional false)))

nil
